bchill@gis.ucdavis. (Brian C Hill) writes:

>	It appears that if you export file systems via a netgroup from
>any system (SunOS, OSF1, Irix, etc.) to an OSF1 3.X system and expect
>to be able to access any of those systems from the OSF 3.X via the
>-hosts map of the automounter, you have to have the netgroup on the OSF
>3.X system as well!

>	Is this correct? If so, does Digital see this as a bug in its
>automounter? Is it known? Will it be fixed?

From a quick look at the code, I'd say your analysis completely correct
and I guess I'd call it a bug.  However, I don't see it getting fixed
any time soon.  In our environment, we have many large servers that
export several file systems only to the other production machines via
a netgroup.  I assume the intent of that code (I don't know if
we wrote it of if it came from Sun) is to reduce the amount of time
automount needs to mount everything from server.  As long as we keep
using automount, there's a lot to be said for reducing its workload,
at least for the automounts that run on the production machines.
